# Git & PR Conventions. We use a universal glob because version control happens regardless of the file extension being edited, but keep it probabilistic so it only loads when the prompt explicitly mentions commits or PRs.

Whenever generating git commit messages or GitHub CLI commands (`gh pr create`):
1. Always extract the ticket ID (e.g., ACME-142) from the provided issue document.
2. Prefix the commit message and PR title with the ticket ID (e.g., `ACME-142: Add high_boost_filter`).
3. Include a brief summary of the ticket in the PR body.
